Write the migration pair db/migrations/0063_customer_tax_fields.up.sql and .down.sql for the billing service (PostgreSQL 15).

Up:
- ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN tax_id text NULL;
- ADD COLUMN tax_exempt boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false;
- ADD COLUMN tax_country char(2) NULL;
- CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY customers_tax_country_idx ON customers (tax_country);

Because of the CONCURRENTLY index, the up file must start with the line `-- no-transaction` (our runner's marker) and must not contain BEGIN/COMMIT.

Down: drop the index with DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS, then drop the three columns, also with `-- no-transaction` on the first line.

Follow the formatting of 0062_*.sql (lowercase keywords are not used there; match whatever it does). Run `make migrate-lint` and fix anything it flags in your two files only. The migration will be reviewed in the PR before it runs anywhere.
